cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PostgreSQL Polaris or its synthetic dataset in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "PostgreSQL Polaris: a reproducible PostgreSQL curriculum and synthetic urban dataset with planted ground truth"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Praveen
    given-names: Satvik
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/Postgres-Polaris"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - PostgreSQL
  - PostGIS
  - synthetic data
  - reproducibility
  - benchmarking
  - database education
  - anomaly detection
abstract: >-
  PostgreSQL Polaris is a containerised PostgreSQL 17/18 environment with a
  deterministic, scalable synthetic city dataset (civics, commerce, mobility,
  geography, documents) generated in SQL with a counter-based RNG. The dataset
  carries planted effects with known parameters and labelled anomalies, so
  analytical and detection methods can be validated against ground truth.
  Sixteen modules cover schema design through MVCC, query tuning, security,
  replication and capstone analyses; a pgTAP suite, a module isolation checker,
  a fingerprint-based reproducibility check and a pgbench harness with
  confidence intervals run in CI.
